<title>USA: U.S. steel centers ship 26.89 million tons in 1996.</title>
<headline>U.S. steel centers ship 26.89 million tons in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. steel service centers shipped 26.89 million tons in 1996, just 0.94 percent below the previous year's level, Steel Service Center Institute reported.</p>
<p>&quot;The second half of 1996 outperformed the last two quarters of 1995, which is just the opposite of what happened during the first half,&quot; said SSCI president David R Roland.</p>
<p>In December, the average daily shipping rate fell 12.6 percent from November due to maintenance and holiday schedules, the institute added.</p>
<p>Shipments in 1997 should be similar to 1994's total of 26.3 million tons, the institute said.</p>
<p>((New York Commodities 212-859-1646))</p>
